# saphira-pbx-mcp runtime identity (canonical, fixed): user
# saphira-pbx-mcp UID 155, primary group saphira-pbx-mcp GID 155,
# home /var/empty (the network half is stateless), shell nologin.
# Only the `mcp serve` network frontend runs as this identity: the
# daemon starts as root (bind, key material, root-only state) and
# drops the frontend itself after fork; the backend stays root.
# UID/GID 155 is the first free ID above asterisk 154, inside the
# preferred 0..199 range - never reuse it for another identity.
# State directories: the backend owns /var/lib/saphira-pbx, mode
# 0711 (traverse without list, never relaxed): the asterisk identity
# must reach generated configuration it owns at 0640, while listing
# and all other access stay denied; DB/WAL/SHM stay 0600 root.
# Proven: 0700 made every generation unreadable to the daemon
# (pbx_config declined at boot, all reloads failed).
# /etc/saphira-pbx holds the transport config; /etc/saphira-pbx/tls
# is group-traversable so the staged key (root:saphira-pbx-mcp 0640,
# never world-visible) stays readable to the service group. Each leaf
# is reconciled by the platform reconciler (never walked), hence
# every leaf is declared explicitly.
user saphira-pbx-mcp 155 saphira-pbx-mcp /var/empty /sbin/nologin
group saphira-pbx-mcp 155
dir /var/lib/saphira-pbx 0711 root root
dir /etc/saphira-pbx 0750 root root
dir /etc/saphira-pbx/tls 0750 root saphira-pbx-mcp
